> (A.stoppedHist O X Y ω, out ω)) P)\n    (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun ω => (A.stoppedHist O' X' Y' ω, out' ω)) P') =\n  InformationTheory.klDiv (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (A.stoppedHist O X Y) P)\n    (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (A.stoppedHist O' X' Y') P')","conclusionHead":"Eq","conclusionRefs":[[0,23,"InformationTheory.klDiv"],[25,50,"MeasureTheory.Measure.map"],[64,75,"Learning.IdentAlg.stoppedHist"],[101,126,"MeasureTheory.Measure.map"],[140,151,"Learning.IdentAlg.stoppedHist"],[177,178,"Eq"],[181,204,"InformationTheory.klDiv"],[206,231,"MeasureTheory.Measure.map"],[235,246,"Learning.IdentAlg.stoppedHist"],[262,287,"MeasureTheory.Measure.map"],[291,302,"Learning.IdentAlg.stoppedHist"]],"decl":"Learning.IdentAlg.IsRun.klDiv_map_stoppedHist_out"},"code":"/-- **Data processing for runs**: for two runs of the same identification algorithm, the\ndivergence between the laws of the pairs (history at the stopping time, output) is the divergence\nbetween the laws of the histories at the stopping time. -/\nlemma IsRun.klDiv_map_stoppedHist_out (h : A.IsRun env O X Y out P)\n    (h' : A.IsRun env' O' X' Y' out' P') :\n    klDiv (P.map fun ω ↦ (A.stoppedHist O X Y ω, out ω))\n        (P'.map fun ω ↦ (A.stoppedHist O' X' Y' ω, out' ω)) =\n      klDiv (P.map (A.stoppedHist O X Y)) (P'.map (A.stoppedHist O' X' Y'))","proof":":= by\n  rw [h.hasCondDistrib_output.map_eq, h'.hasCondDistrib_output.map_eq]\n  exact klDiv_compProd_left _ _ _","source":{"path":"Maiti2026Power/LeanMachineLearning/RunDivergence.lean","start":44,"end":53,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/colt-2026-83/blob/3f6c0f296a3b7e4aa8fe333225505f5b2f61f9e0/Maiti2026Power/LeanMachineLearning/RunDivergence.lean#L44-L53"},"deps":[],"outside":[],"external":[["ENNReal","mathlib","definition"],["Eq","lean4","inductive"],["Fin","lean4","structure"],["InformationTheory.klDiv","mathlib","definition"],["Learning.Environment","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.Hist","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["Learning.IdentAlg","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IdentAlg.IsRun","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IdentAlg.stoppedHist","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["Learning.Round","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["MeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["MeasurableSpace.pi","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.Measure","mathlib","structure"],["MeasureTheory.Measure.map","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.instIsZeroOrProbabilityMeasureOfIsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["Nat","lean4","inductive"],["PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Prod","lean4","structure"],["Prod.instMeasurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Prod.mk","lean4","constructor"],["Sigma","lean4","structure"],["Sigma.instMeasurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Unit","lean4","definition"]],"users":[],"sorry":false,"ownSorry":false,"sorryVia":[],"axioms":[],"change":null,"reviews":[],"claim":null,"specifies":[],"specifiedBy":[],"characterizations":[],"pulled":false,"directExternal":["ENNReal","Eq","Fin","InformationTheory.klDiv","Learning.Environment","Learning.Hist","Learning.IdentAlg","Learning.IdentAlg.IsRun","Learning.IdentAlg.stoppedHist","Learning.Round","MeasurableSpace","MeasurableSpace.pi","MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","MeasureTheory.Measure","MeasureTheory.Measure.map","MeasureTheory.instIsZeroOrProbabilityMeasureOfIsProbabilityMeasure","Nat","PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","Prod","Prod.instMeasurableSpace","Prod.mk","Sigma","Sigma.instMeasurableSpace","Unit"],"provenance":null,"edited":{"commit":"f1a92e33571fde49fce6355928bb1a73476e5a39","date":"2026-09-13"}},{"id":275,"name":"Learning.IdentAlg.IsRun.klDiv_map_out_le_lintegral","kind":"Lemma","keyword":"lemma","module":"Maiti2026Power.LeanMachineLearning.RunDivergence","package":"Maiti2026Power","isProp":true,"hashes":{"meaning":"995c0ba0345514b8","local":"d64f21aafd0bee0b","content":"5c4948c5e276124e"},"doc":"**Change of measure at a stopping time**, integral form: for two runs of the same\nidentification algorithm in two stationary environments with reward kernels `κ` and `κ'`, with\nalmost surely finite stopping times, the divergence between the laws of the outputs is at most\nthe expected sum, along the first run, of the divergences of the reward kernels at the actions\nplayed before stopping. ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓐","role":"type","type":"Type u_1","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓨","role":"type","type":"Type u_2","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓓","role":"type","type":"Type u_3","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓐","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓨","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓨","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓓","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓓","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_4","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Ω'","role":"type","type":"Type u_5","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"mΩ","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"mΩ'","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω'","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.Measure","implicit":true,"name":"P","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω","typeRefs":[[0,21,"MeasureTheory.Measure"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.Measur